{"meetingId": "937", "tickets": [
{"title": "Coordinate Divorce Document Package", "templateId": "d0a74fb4-d997-51d3-a171-f40e13c7dd68", "text": "Use this coordination template when Liora Velvetreed needs help organizing financial documents related to divorce proceedings in Multnomah County Circuit Court. Maintain confidentiality, avoid legal advice, and route documents only to authorized parties. Assemble approved account, income, debt, insurance, estate, and beneficiary records for Sela Fablethimble of Moonbadger Legal, with sharing limited to the divorce matter.", "priority": "high", "dueDate": "2024-03-08", "assigneeId": null, "subTasks": [
{"title": "Intake authorization and document list", "text": "Confirm authorized contacts, communication limits, and requested document categories such as statements, tax records, income records, insurance, liabilities, and estate documents. Sharing is limited to the divorce matter and routed to Sela Fablethimble of Moonbadger Legal.", "priority": "high", "assigneeId": "b384ec7e-6251-5024-b063-047ec07f91d8", "dueDate": null},
{"title": "Compile financial records", "text": "Collect available account statements, cost basis summaries, cash flow records, beneficiary confirmations, and debt summaries from approved sources for Liora Velvetreed.", "priority": "high", "assigneeId": "b93ee058-c11a-51d8-8005-81fe1e23bd94", "dueDate": null},
{"title": "Review planning implications", "text": "Identify investment, retirement, tax, equity compensation, cash flow, and beneficiary issues that may require advisor discussion or outside professional review.", "priority": "medium", "assigneeId": "4667bc56-66a8-50b5-9e6c-5140770cc465", "dueDate": null},
{"title": "Coordinate secure handoff", "text": "Package approved documents through the secure delivery method and log what was shared, with whom, and under what authorization.", "priority": "high", "assigneeId": "b384ec7e-6251-5024-b063-047ec07f91d8", "dueDate": null}
], "evidence": "For the divorce financial document package, Liora asked Apricot Compass Advisory to assemble approved account, income, debt, insurance, estate, and beneficiary records for Sela Fablethimble at Moonbadger Legal, with sharing limited to the divorce matter. The agreed follow-up is due March 8, 2024."},
{"title": "Review Access Recovery Evidence", "templateId": "e968965a-969b-53fe-a5d3-3b7ff9150636", "text": "Review the access recovery request for Liora Velvetreed using these criteria and evidence points: Devin still appears to have visibility into a joint secure vault folder, and Liora received an e-signature error when attempting to upload the temporary order. Confirm whether access should be restored, reset, limited, transferred, or revoked, and check contact information and permissions on file.", "priority": "high", "dueDate": "2024-03-05", "assigneeId": null, "subTasks": [], "evidence": "The agreed follow-up, due March 5, 2024, is to review access, contact information, and permissions."},
{"title": "Request missing divorce records through legal channel", "templateId": null, "text": "Request the missing divorce records for Liora Velvetreed through the authorized legal channel: current statements for Devin's retirement plan (Marzipan Meadow Textiles plan, last statement $415,000 on September 30, 2023), Buttonwood Balloon Studio distribution history, and the home equity line freeze notice.", "priority": null, "dueDate": "2024-03-12", "assigneeId": null, "subTasks": [], "evidence": "The agreed follow-up is to request the records through the authorized legal channel by March 12, 2024."},
{"title": "Reconcile mortgage balance for marital balance sheet", "templateId": null, "text": "Check the source documents for the Portland residence mortgage serviced by Coral Badger Lending, where the legal worksheet shows a $411,000 payoff while the portal shows $424,880 of principal, and update the marital balance sheet for Liora Velvetreed with the verified figure.", "priority": null, "dueDate": "2024-03-11", "assigneeId": null, "subTasks": [], "evidence": "The agreed follow-up, due March 11, 2024, is to check the source documents and update the marital balance sheet with the verified figure."},
{"title": "Prepare settlement conference planning figures", "templateId": null, "text": "Prepare a marital balance sheet and sustainable cash flow view for Liora Velvetreed before the settlement conference, including home-retention scenarios, support payments, legal fees, and tax-sensitive sale assumptions. She pays $2,800 per month in interim household support, estimates $9,400 per month in household spending, and prefers nine months of essential expenses in liquid accounts.", "priority": null, "dueDate": "2024-03-29", "assigneeId": null, "subTasks": [], "evidence": "The court schedule requires a marital balance sheet and sustainable cash flow view before the settlement conference, including home-retention scenarios, support payments, legal fees, and tax-sensitive sale assumptions. The agreed follow-up is due March 29, 2024."},
{"title": "Prepare ownership and beneficiary review comments", "templateId": null, "text": "Prepare adviser comments for attorney review for Liora Velvetreed covering account titling, beneficiary designations, trustee roles, and insurance ownership affected by the separation, including the 2016 joint revocable trust with Devin as co-trustee and the $1.5 million Silver Marmot Insurance term life policy naming Devin as primary beneficiary, before any legal or custodial changes are made.", "priority": null, "dueDate": "2024-03-22", "assigneeId": null, "subTasks": [], "evidence": "The agreed follow-up, due March 22, 2024, is to prepare adviser comments for attorney review before any legal or custodial changes are made."},
{"title": "Review Concentrated Position", "templateId": "b835d25d-d355-5804-8593-94348f4d26b8", "text": "Evaluate the Paper Otter Robotics concentrated position for Liora Velvetreed for portfolio risk, tax exposure, liquidity needs, restrictions, and diversification options. Vested shares in the taxable account at Velvet Acorn Custody are valued at about $690,000 with an estimated cost basis of $210,000, roughly 28% of investable assets, plus $310,000 in unvested RSUs. Model staged sale, retention, gifting, and reinvestment alternatives with attention to liquidity needs and divorce restrictions.", "priority": "high", "dueDate": "2024-03-18", "assigneeId": "4667bc56-66a8-50b5-9e6c-5140770cc465", "subTasks": [
{"title": "Assemble Position Facts", "text": "Collect current market value, share count, cost basis, acquisition history, holding period, account registration, and any employer equity plan details for the Paper Otter Robotics position. Confirm whether blackout windows, lockups, Rule 144, or insider restrictions may apply.", "priority": "high", "assigneeId": "47926d53-db41-532d-99c2-224dc3aaa5ea", "dueDate": null},
{"title": "Model Portfolio and Tax Impact", "text": "Analyze concentration percentage, sector exposure, volatility, unrealized gain or loss, charitable giving opportunities, tax-loss offsets, and estimated tax impact under phased-sale scenarios for the Paper Otter Robotics holdings.", "priority": "high", "assigneeId": "96c9c35b-0519-5544-bd5f-e8e441dccdb2", "dueDate": null},
{"title": "Draft Diversification Recommendation", "text": "Prepare a client-ready summary comparing hold, trim, staged sale, gifting, hedging, and reinvestment options. Include key assumptions, open questions for the CPA or attorney, and next-step implementation considerations.", "priority": "medium", "assigneeId": "4667bc56-66a8-50b5-9e6c-5140770cc465", "dueDate": null}
], "evidence": "The agreed follow-up, due March 18, 2024, is to model staged sale, retention, gifting, and reinvestment alternatives with attention to liquidity needs and divorce restrictions."},
{"title": "Prepare Cash Distribution Request", "templateId": "bbc351a0-d7f3-59a9-9b6e-c1705881ee7f", "text": "Distribution purpose: Legal retainer and near-term living costs\nRequested gross or net amount: $35,000 net\nSource account type: Joint taxable investment account at Velvet Acorn Custody\nPreferred delivery method: [ACH / check / wire / internal transfer]\nReceiving account or payee placeholder: Liora Velvetreed's separate checking account at Teacup Comet Bank\nTax withholding instruction, if applicable: [Federal / state / none / discuss]\nFrequency: One-time\nLiquidity source to review: [Money market / sale proceeds / scheduled income / other]\nClient authorization method: [Portal / signed form / recorded instruction / other]\nSpecial notes: Subject to available cash, tax lot review, and required authorization.\n\nBefore processing, confirm available cash, tax considerations, required forms, and whether the request affects the client's plan assumptions.", "priority": "medium", "dueDate": "2024-03-06", "assigneeId": null, "subTasks": [], "evidence": "Liora requested a one-time $35,000 net transfer from the joint taxable account to her separate Teacup Comet Bank checking account for a legal retainer and near-term living costs, subject to available cash, tax lot review, and required authorization. The agreed follow-up is due March 6, 2024."}
]}
